CAT = "zare5Debar"; SEG = "DEB"
Q = [
("Debarment of a representative means the FSP:",
 "Stops them serving clients", ["Fines them for poor sales", "Suspends its own licence", "Moves them to admin work"],
 "Debarment removes a person's ability to render financial services as a representative and their name from the registers."),
("What is the main purpose of debarment?",
 "To protect clients", ["To punish poor sales figures", "To cut the FSP's commission costs", "To enforce a restraint of trade"],
 "Debarment protects clients and the integrity of the industry by stopping people who are not fit and proper from rendering financial services."),
("An FSP must debar a representative who:",
 "Is no longer fit and proper", ["Has missed a sales target", "Has left to join a rival", "Has taken extended unpaid leave"],
 "Section 14 requires an FSP to debar a representative who no longer meets the fit and proper requirements, or who has contravened the Act in a material manner."),
("An FSP must also debar a representative who has:",
 "Materially broken the FAIS Act", ["Received a client compliment", "Moved to part-time work", "Changed product suppliers"],
 "A material contravention of the Act is the second ground for debarment in section 14."),
("Before debarring a representative, the FSP must:",
 "Give written notice", ["Get the Ombud's prior approval", "Obtain a court order", "Consult the rep's clients"],
 "The FSP must give the representative adequate prior written notice of its intention to debar and the grounds and reasons for it."),
("During the debarment process, the representative must be given a chance to:",
 "Respond before the decision", ["Choose their replacement", "Collect future commission", "Appoint a new key individual"],
 "The FSP must give the representative a reasonable opportunity to make a submission and must consider it before deciding."),
("Before debarring a representative, the FSP must give them a copy of:",
 "Its debarment policy", ["Its annual financial statements", "Every client's file", "Its licence application"],
 "Section 14(3)(a)(ii) of the FAIS Act requires the FSP to provide a copy of its written policy and procedure governing the debarment process."),
("When the FSP decides to debar, it must tell the representative about:",
 "Their right to reconsideration", ["Their right to a fee refund", "The FSP's sales results", "Their new employer's details"],
 "Section 14(3)(c) of the FAIS Act requires the FSP to notify the person in writing of the decision, their rights under Chapter 15 of the FSR Act and the requirements for reconsideration by the Tribunal."),
("After debarring a representative, the FSP must:",
 "Delete them from its register", ["Keep them listed as active", "Let them finish current deals", "Transfer their clients to them"],
 "The FSP must immediately remove the debarred person from its register of representatives."),
("After a debarment, the FSP must notify:",
 "The Authority", ["The representative's family", "Every product supplier", "The Financial Intelligence Centre"],
 "Section 14(4) of the FAIS Act requires the FSP to notify the Authority within five days of the debarment and to give the grounds and reasons within 15 days."),
("When a representative is debarred, the FSP must make sure that the representative's clients:",
 "Are still properly looked after", ["Are told to complain to the Ombud", "Cancel their policies", "Follow the representative"],
 "Section 14(4)(c) of the FAIS Act requires the FSP to take steps immediately so that the debarment does not prejudice the debarred person's clients and that unconcluded business is properly attended to."),
("Apart from an FSP, may the Authority itself debar a person?",
 "Yes, under the FSR Act", ["No, only the FSP can", "Only with a court order", "Only the Ombud can"],
 "Section 153 of the Financial Sector Regulation Act lets the Authority debar a person, for example for serious contraventions of a financial sector law."),
("A debarred representative disagrees with the decision. They may:",
 "Apply to the Tribunal", ["Appeal to the Ombud for FSPs", "Ask the FIC to reverse it", "Ask the product supplier"],
 "Debarment decisions can be taken to the Financial Services Tribunal for reconsideration under the Financial Sector Regulation Act."),
("A debarred person may be appointed as a representative again only if:",
 "They are fit and proper again", ["A new FSP is willing to appoint them", "One year has passed", "A client asks for them"],
 "Reappointment is possible only once the person again meets the fit and proper requirements, including any exam and qualification requirements."),
("A representative forges a client's signature on an application. The FSP should:",
 "Start the debarment process", ["Give a verbal warning", "Reduce the rep's commission", "Wait for a complaint"],
 "Forgery shows a lack of honesty and integrity and is a material contravention, so the FSP must start the section 14 debarment process."),
("A representative resigns while the FSP is looking into serious misconduct. The FSP:",
 "May still debar them", ["Loses its power to act", "Must ask the Ombud to act", "Must refund their commission"],
 "Section 14(1) of the FAIS Act covers a person who is or was a representative, if the reasons arose while they were one. Section 14(5) requires such a debarment to start within six months after they left."),
]
